4.3 Key Components

The solution consists of the following major components:

Raw Layer

Stores the latest source data received from upstream systems.

Previous Raw Layer

Maintains the previous execution's source data to enable comparison with the current data.

Staging Layer

Performs row-level change detection by identifying Inserts, Updates, and Deletes before downstream processing.

History Layer

Maintains complete historical versions of business records using the Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2 (SCD Type 2) methodology.

Snapshot Layer

Maintains the latest version of each business record for reporting and downstream consumption.

Logging Framework

Captures execution details including processing status, timestamps, execution duration, record counts, retry information, and error details.

Audit Framework

Provides operational visibility and enables monitoring, validation, and troubleshooting of pipeline executions.

4.4 Key Features

The proposed framework introduces several enhancements:

Automated incremental processing
Row-level change detection
Historical data preservation
Current-state snapshot generation
Parallel processing
Retry mechanism
Automated backfill processing
Comprehensive logging
Audit reporting
Metadata-driven execution
Error handling and recovery
Scalability across hundreds of source tables
4.5 Benefits

The implementation provides several operational and business benefits.

Improved Performance

Parallel execution significantly reduces overall processing time compared to sequential processing.

Increased Reliability

Retry mechanisms and comprehensive error handling improve pipeline stability.

Better Data Quality

Standardized change detection ensures accurate processing of Inserts, Updates, and Deletes.

Complete Historical Tracking

Historical records are preserved for reporting, auditing, and regulatory purposes.

Operational Visibility

Detailed logs provide complete insight into execution status and processing metrics.

Scalability

The metadata-driven framework allows new tables to be onboarded without major code changes.

Simplified Maintenance

Reusable processing logic reduces code duplication and simplifies future enhancements.

